.TH APPSCAN 1 "September 2026" "appscan 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
appscan \- scan with the Epson Perfection 2480/2580 PHOTO on Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B appscan
.RB [ gui ]
.br
.B appscan scan
.I OUTPUT
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B appscan list
.br
.B appscan warmup
.br
.B appscan reset
.br
.B appscan firmware
.br
.B appscan
.BR \-\-version " | " \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B appscan
is a command\-line tool and Tk graphical interface for the Epson Perfection
2480 PHOTO and 2580 PHOTO flatbed scanners.
It is a thin layer over the
.B snapscan
backend of SANE: every scan is performed by
.BR scanimage (1),
driven with a private SANE configuration that
.B appscan
writes itself.
No changes to
.I /etc/sane.d
are needed and nothing has to run as root.
.PP
These scanners need Epson's firmware uploaded every time they are powered on.
Run
.B appscan firmware
once to download and install it; after that, the upload happens automatically
the first time the scanner is used after power\-on.
Until the firmware is installed, every command except
.B firmware
and
.B reset
fails with an error, and the GUI cannot scan.
.PP
Without a command,
.B appscan
opens the graphical interface.
It offers drop\-down lists for source, mode, resolution and depth, sliders for
brightness and contrast (\-100 to 100 in steps of 5, disabled in
.B Lineart
mode; double\-click a slider to reset it), a
.B Preview
button (a colour scan of the whole area at 50\ dpi), and an area selection
made by dragging on the preview; without a selection the whole area is scanned.
.B Scan\&...\&
asks where to save the file; as with
.BR "appscan scan" ,
its extension selects the format.
Multi\-page PDF documents are built with
.BR "Add page" ,
.B "Save PDF\&...\&"
and
.BR Discard ;
while pages are waiting to be saved the resolution cannot be changed.
A progress bar and a
.B Cancel
button follow the running scan.
On start the GUI warms up the lamp in the background; the scan buttons stay
disabled until it is done.
Closing the window, or pressing
.B Ctrl\-C
in the terminal that started it, cancels a running scan (or waits for a file
being written), and asks first if PDF pages have not been saved.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B gui
Open the graphical interface.
This is the default when no command is given.
.TP
.BI scan " OUTPUT"
Scan to the file
.IR OUTPUT .
The file type is chosen by its extension; see
.B "Options for scan"
below.
Progress is printed on standard error.
.B Ctrl\-C
cancels the scan; if it is cancelled before image data starts flowing, or the
cancel does not finish within 10 seconds, the scanner is reset and its lamp
must warm up again.
.TP
.B list
List the detected scanners by SANE device name, for example
.BR snapscan:libusb:001:011 ,
or print
.B No scanner found
if there is none.
The bus and device numbers change whenever the scanner is replugged.
.TP
.B warmup
Switch the lamp on and wait until it is warm, so that the next scan starts
immediately.
A cold lamp needs about 30\(en40 seconds after power\-on or a reset.
.TP
.B reset
Reset the scanner's USB connection when it stops responding, which has the
same effect as unplugging and replugging it.
The lamp needs to warm up again afterwards.
.TP
.B firmware
Download Epson's Windows driver from
.br
\%https://ftp.epson.com/drivers/epson12204.exe,
.br
extract
.I esfw41.bin
from it, verify its SHA\-256 checksum and install it.
The same file serves both the 2480 and the 2580.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Global options"
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version number and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
Also accepted after a command, as in
.BR "appscan scan \-h" .
.SS "Options for scan"
.TP
.I OUTPUT
The file to write.
Its extension selects the format:
.BR .png ,
.B .jpg
or
.BR .jpeg ,
.B .tif
or
.BR .tiff ,
.BR .pnm ,
.BR .pdf ,
in upper or lower case.
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR {\fBColor\fR|\fBGray\fR|\fBLineart\fR}
Colour mode.
.B Lineart
produces pure black and white, suited to text and fax\-like documents;
it ignores
.BR \-\-brightness ,
.B \-\-contrast
and
.BR \-\-depth .
Default:
.BR Color .
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-resolution\fR \fIDPI\fR
Resolution in dots per inch; one of 50, 75, 100, 150, 200, 300, 400, 600,
1200 or 2400.
Default: 300.
.TP
\fB\-\-depth\fR {\fB8\fR|\fB16\fR}
Bits per colour channel.
A depth of 16 needs
.BR .png ,
.B .tif
(or
.BR .tiff )
or
.B .pnm
output; with
.B .jpg
or
.B .jpeg
it is an error, even in
.B Lineart
mode.
The depth is ignored in
.B Lineart
mode and for
.B .pdf
output.
Default: 8.
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR {\fBFlatbed\fR|\fB"Transparency Adapter"\fR}
Where to scan from.
The transparency adapter is the unit for film and slides; its scan area is
55\(mu125\ mm on the 2480 (see
.B BUGS
for the 2580).
Quote the value in the shell, since it contains a space.
Default:
.BR Flatbed .
.TP
\fB\-\-area\fR \fILEFT TOP WIDTH HEIGHT\fR
The area to scan, in millimetres, measured from the top\-left corner of the
scan area of the source.
Decimal values are accepted.
Default: the whole scan area of the source (216\(mu297\ mm on the flatbed).
.TP
\fB\-\-brightness\fR \fIPERCENT\fR
Brightness adjustment, a whole number from \-400 to 400.
Ignored in
.B Lineart
mode.
Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-contrast\fR \fIPERCENT\fR
Contrast adjustment, a whole number from \-100 to 400.
Ignored in
.B Lineart
mode.
Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-pages\fR \fIN\fR
Only for PDF output: scan
.I N
pages into one PDF file.
A value other than 1 with an output that is not
.BR .pdf ,
or a value below 1, is a usage error.
Before each page after the first,
.B appscan
waits for Enter on standard input, giving you time to place the next sheet.
Stopping early, with
.B Ctrl\-C
or end of input (\fBCtrl\-D\fR), still saves the pages scanned so far;
if no page has been scanned yet, nothing is saved and the scan counts as
cancelled.
If a page fails, the pages scanned before it are saved too, and the error is
reported afterwards.
Default: 1.
.PP
The folder of
.I OUTPUT
must be writable; this is checked before scanning starts.
.PP
PDF output ignores
.BR \-\-depth :
colour and grey pages are 8 bits per channel and JPEG\-compressed, and a PDF
made only of
.B Lineart
pages is 1 bit per pixel and lossless.
A PDF that mixes
.B Lineart
pages with colour or grey pages (possible in the GUI) stores them all as
JPEG.
An existing file is replaced only once the new PDF has been written
completely.
.B appscan
assembles the PDF itself from the scanned pages, and each page size matches
the scanned area at the chosen resolution.
.SH EXAMPLES
Quick colour scan of a document at the default 300\ dpi:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan scan letter.png
.EE
.RE
.PP
Greyscale scan at 600\ dpi:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan scan \-\-mode Gray \-r 600 page.png
.EE
.RE
.PP
Crop a 15\(mu10\ cm photo lying 20\ mm from the left edge and 30\ mm from the
top of the glass, saved as a JPEG:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan scan \-r 600 \-\-area 20 30 150 100 holiday.jpg
.EE
.RE
.PP
Archival scan of a photo as a 16\-bit TIFF:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan scan \-r 1200 \-\-depth 16 \-\-area 0 0 130 180 grandma.tif
.EE
.RE
.PP
Film or slides through the transparency adapter of a 2480 at 2400\ dpi
(the whole 55\(mu125\ mm area in 16\-bit colour is about 370\ MB):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan scan \-\-source "Transparency Adapter" \-r 2400 \e
    \-\-depth 16 \-\-area 0 0 55 125 film\-01.tif
.EE
.RE
.PP
A four\-page contract in one PDF; press Enter after placing each new sheet:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan scan \-\-mode Gray \-r 200 \-\-pages 4 contract.pdf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Brighten a faded page and raise its contrast:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan scan \-\-brightness 30 \-\-contrast 40 faded.png
.EE
.RE
.PP
Lineart at 300\ dpi for plain text or fax\-like documents:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan scan \-\-mode Lineart \-r 300 memo.png
.EE
.RE
.PP
Warm the lamp up first in a script, so the scans start without delay:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
#!/bin/sh
set \-e
appscan warmup
appscan scan \-r 600 cover.png
appscan scan \-r 600 back.png
.EE
.RE
.PP
Batch loop naming each file by date and time; type
.B q
at the prompt to stop:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan warmup
while :; do
    f="receipt\-$(date +%Y%m%d\-%H%M%S).png"
    appscan scan \-\-mode Gray \-r 200 "$f" || break
    printf \(aqPlace the next sheet, then Enter (q to quit): \(aq
    read \-r answer || break
    [ "$answer" = q ] && break
done
.EE
.RE
.PP
Recover when the scanner stops answering:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan reset
appscan warmup
appscan scan retry.png
.EE
.RE
.PP
List the connected scanners:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ appscan list
snapscan:libusb:001:011
.EE
.RE
.PP
Install the firmware (needed once, before the first scan):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
appscan firmware
.EE
.RE
.PP
Collect backend debug output for a scan that fails
.RB ( appscan
reports the messages of
.BR scanimage (1),
debug lines included, only when the scan fails):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
SANE_DEBUG_SNAPSCAN=30 appscan scan test.png 2> snapscan.log
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/appscan/
Data directory; defaults to
.IR \(ti/.local/share/appscan/ .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/appscan/esfw41.bin
The scanner firmware, installed by
.BR "appscan firmware" .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/appscan/sane.d/
Private SANE configuration
.RI ( dll.conf ,
.IR snapscan.conf ,
and an empty
.I dll.d/
directory), written again whenever
.B appscan
needs the scanner.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/applications/appscan.desktop
Desktop menu entry, installed by
.IR install.sh .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/appscan.svg
Application icon, installed by
.IR install.sh .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/man/man1/appscan.1
This manual page, installed by
.IR install.sh .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for data files; ignored unless it is an absolute path.
Default:
.IR \(ti/.local/share .
.B appscan
cannot use the scanner if its data directory contains a
.B :
or a
.BR \(dq .
.TP
.B SANE_DEBUG_SNAPSCAN
Passed on to
.BR scanimage (1)
to enable debug output from the snapscan backend, for example
.BR SANE_DEBUG_SNAPSCAN=30 .
.TP
.B SANE_CONFIG_DIR
Set by
.B appscan
itself when it runs
.BR scanimage (1),
replacing any value already set: it points at the private configuration,
with
.I /etc/sane.d
as the fallback.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including a multi\-page scan stopped early that saved at least one
page.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred, such as an unsupported output file type, a scanner that
does not answer, or a failing page in a multi\-page scan (the pages before it
are still saved); or the scan was cancelled with
.BR Ctrl\-C .
.TP
.B 2
Invalid usage, such as an unknown option, a value that is not one of the
choices or out of range,
.B \-\-pages
without a
.B .pdf
output, or an output folder that is not writable.
.SH INSTALLATION
.B appscan
is installed as a
.B uv
tool.
To install it, together with the desktop entry, icon and this manual page,
and to download the firmware:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
curl \-fsSL \e
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/matteospanio/appscan/main/install.sh \e
| bash
.EE
.RE
.PP
Missing system packages
.RB ( sane\-utils ,
.BR curl ,
.BR p7zip\-full ,
.BR cabextract ,
.BR python3\-tk )
are installed with
.B sudo apt\-get
when available.
Set
.B \%APPSCAN_SKIP_FIRMWARE=1
to skip the firmware download; if it is skipped or fails, run
.B appscan firmware
later.
.PP
To uninstall it, together with the data directory and the firmware:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
curl \-fsSL \e
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/matteospanio/appscan/main/install.sh \e
| bash \-s \-\- \-\-uninstall
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
The first open after power\-on uploads the firmware.
With sane\-backends 1.1.1 this open often fails once;
.B appscan
retries automatically.
.PP
After power\-on or a USB reset the lamp needs about 30\(en40 seconds to warm
up, while later scans start within a few seconds.
Run
.B appscan warmup
ahead of time to avoid the wait.
.PP
If the scanner is plugged in but not answering,
.B appscan
resets it automatically before giving up.
.PP
Brightness and contrast range from \-100 to 100 in the GUI, a narrower range
than the command line accepts.
.SH BUGS
Cancelling before image data flows (during the firmware upload or warm\-up),
or a cancel that hangs in the backend for more than 10 seconds (which happens
about one time in three), makes
.B appscan
kill
.BR scanimage (1)
and reset the scanner.
.PP
SANE reports the film unit of the 2580 as unsupported.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scanimage (1),
.BR sane\-snapscan (5),
.BR sane (7)
